  "claimBoundary": "Design artifact only. This instance is a hand-authored worked example of the C1 review-policy contract, built on the motivating example of proposal section 1.7 (p.9): the Model Inspector reports an added actor 'Shift Supervisor', not named in the domain text, mediating two relations that other submissions attach directly to the operator, and six readings of that one fragment remain live. It exists to show how claim-specific assessed competence and claim-specific asserted authority are carried as two separately evidenced inputs: here the modeling-language specialist holds the highest assessed competence (0.91) on the notation reading and an advisory mandate only, while the instructor who owns the rubric holds the lowest assessed competence (0.48) and the only mandate that reaches the guideline-gap reading, so the joint selection function routes to the instructor. Every identifier, score, weight, threshold, budget figure, and reviewer attribute is illustrative and invented for documentation; every SHA-256 is the hash of a documented placeholder string prefixed 'review-policy-signal-contract-v1/example/placeholder/' and refers to no real frozen document, log, or registry. No important-case capture, selective-risk, burden, interruption-cost, or accuracy value has been measured, and the two label fields are deliberately left at not_yet_established and not_yet_evaluated. importantCaseLabelIndependentOfPolicy is recorded as false because no label exists over which independence could be asserted, not because a label was derived from a routing decision. Validation of this file against ReviewPolicySignalContract-v1 is evidence about the schema, not evidence about any outcome."
